/* asic/spice/pads.py: the PDK's sg13g2_io_slow_1p08V_3p0V_125C.lib, with the timing of
     sg13g2_IOPadInOut16mA
     sg13g2_IOPadTriOut16mA
     sg13g2_IOPadOut16mA
     sg13g2_IOPadIn
   as z80_chip.v ties them re-measured at transistor level (ngspice; the
   PDK's netlist and ss models, 125 C, 1.08 V core / 3 V I/O): outputs
   into 1-250 pF beyond the pin's own capacitance, inputs with edges to
   120 ns. Delays 50 % to 50 %, slews 10-90 %, as the PDK's; disable: the
   driver's current under 10 %. The pins' max_transition / max_capacitance:
   the ranges simulated (the pin's edges to 120 ns, past every output edge
   into 250 pF; an output's load to 250 pF beyond its own; the core side's
   to the tables' last points). Internal power: the supplies' energy in the same
   runs, the PDK's way (a rise less the C V^2 that charges the load), with the load
   as STA takes it -- the pin's own capacitance too, half of its C V^2 off each
   edge -- so that STA's internal plus switching power is the simulated energy;
   leakage: each state's DC power. Generated; do not edit. */
